{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924390-effects-of-vampires-drinking-from-supernatural-beings","id":924390,"title":"Effects of Vampires drinking from supernatural beings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-01T04:22:18-07:00","id":924390,"title":"Effects of Vampires drinking from supernatural beings","content":"Reading VTR 1e i found certain outcomes but am curious about others<br /> <br /> \u200bMages- causes hallucinations and derangements, Vitae intake same as normal humans<br /> <br /> Werewolves- increased Vitae intake but more likely to frenzy the next few nights<br /> <br /> Vampires- Needed for high blood potency vampires, possibly increases blood potency if victim had higher blood potency, may cause addiction, derangement roll<br /> <br /> Changling/fae-?<br /> <br /> Prometheans-?<br /> <br /> Beast-? (i know they don't exist in 1e but i am still curious to know)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12063,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","user":"Seta143","date":". 07-01-2016, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:12:18-07:00","id":924416,"title":"","content":"There are 3 other threads on this that list effects. However that said, I don't think any of them include Beast. If it weren't next to impossible to find stuff on here with my phone, I would link them for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:23:52-07:00","id":924419,"title":"","content":"There's nothing canon for Beast, and there never will be, because Beast was released after Vampire 2e came out and supernatural side effects stopped being a thing. <br /> <br /> If I were to homebrew one It would probably involve making the vampire scarier somehow. Maybe something like the Nosferatu curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:43:32-07:00","id":924427,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">All first edition, of course. Changeling blood causes wild hallucinations, fetch blood horrible nightmares and no actual Vitae. Promethean blood tastes awful and gives half the amount taken, so taking 2 Lethal from a Promethean gives the vampire 1 Vitae.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T07:34:02-07:00","id":924442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924390-effects-of-vampires-drinking-from-supernatural-beings?p=924427#post924427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">All first edition, of course.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>None of those effects got translated to the 2e, aside from the impossibility to draw sustenance without a particular merit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T08:45:27-07:00","id":924476,"title":"","content":"Just homebraw your own stuff. I personnally find it dumb that things like werewolf blood don't give you anything except if you have some random merit. Plus, it's practical that it boots you awake like elder blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T08:49:02-07:00","id":924479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924390-effects-of-vampires-drinking-from-supernatural-beings?p=924442#post924442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of those effects got translated to the 2e, aside from the impossibility to draw sustenance without a particular merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP stated 1E. As for second, I homebrew in the effects. It's not game changing and I like the flavor.<br /> <br /> If you are referring to unnatural affinity it is intended for BP 6. Example if you have BP 6 and can only feed on vampires, you take that (werewolves) you can now feed on vampires and werewolves.<br /> <br /> Less than 1-2 you can feed on anything. Including animals, humans, supernaturals<br /> <br /> 3-5 drop animals <br /> <br /> 6 drop everything but vampires unless you take that merit. <br /> <br /> ( there is confirmation in 1 of those 3 threads I mentioned earlier ) <br /> <br /> <br /> Demons are 100% human in their covers and I treat their blood nothing more. In true form it would depend on if they have blood or not.<br /> <br /> Sin eaters- I have had their blood taste dead and allow you to see spirits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T10:38:01-07:00","id":924525,"title":"","content":"In my group, we houseruled unnatural Affinity to be able to specifically be for feeding from entities that you couldn't normally get blood from such as ghosts, spirits, and angels. 2E's conditions are really helpful for working out side-effects of drinking supernatural blood...<br /> <br /> Werewolf = Bestial<br /> Drinking a werewolf's moon-tainted blood brings your Beast closer to the surface.<br /> <br /> Mage = Competitive<br /> Witches are full of a power that transcends reality as you know it. Tasting that power in their blood gives a rush like no other, making you feel like a god.<br /> <br /> Changeling = Wanton<br /> Those touched by Faerie feed on strong emotion, and some of that tempest of feeling is transferred to you when you drink the blood of the Lost.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eater = Lethargic<br /> There's &quot;capital d&quot; Death in the blood of the Bound. Drinking the plams-laced blood of a Sin-Eater makes you feel like you're being dragged down into the grave.<br /> <br /> Demon = Traced<br /> If a vampire feeds on a demon who's Cover is compromised (i.e. afflicted by a condition acquired by failing a Compromise roll), the vampire becomes temporarily susceptible to Compromise. (Wits + Manipulation + Blood Potency for the roll) Resolve the condition when a Compromise roll occurs. Naturally, a vampire doesn't have Cover dots to lose, but a failure or dramatic failure could still attract the attention of the God-Machine and it's hunter angels.<br /> <br /> This approach doesn't work with everything. We made Prometheans dangerous and volatile (and admittedly, maybe a little too complicated). Their pyros is an energy akin to both fire and lightning, but something more vital. It's been a while, but I believe we made it to where a vampire can siphon off pyros while feeding (so a turn of feeding inflicted 1 Lethal on the Prommie and took away 1 pyros, granting 2 Vitae to the vampire). However, the vampire had to keep track of that pyros-Vitae. If the vampire took damage from fire while it still had pyros in its system, there was a chance (we'd roll a number of dice equal to the pyros-Vitae they had, and you'd hope not to get 1s) that the pyros would react to the fire and burn itself away, inflicting even more damage on the vampire. Dangerous stuff.<br /> <br /> As for Beasts... I honestly don't know enough about them to make any specific suggestions, but I do recommend looking for a condition to reflect it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T05:14:54-07:00","id":924846,"title":"","content":"Drinking the blood of supernaturals provided you with the weakness of that supernatural in question. Werewolf rage, mage bedlam insanity, changelings brought a touch of perception difficulty, prometheans inflicted Disquiet. And so on. <br /> <br /> Of course, this is difficult to map to supernaturals (like SinEaters or Beasts) who don't have weaknesses. But its a good starting point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T00:34:45-07:00","id":925783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inkpenavenger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924390-effects-of-vampires-drinking-from-supernatural-beings?p=924525#post924525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my group, we houseruled unnatural Affinity to be able to specifically be for feeding from entities that you couldn't normally get blood from such as ghosts, spirits, and angels. 2E's conditions are really helpful for working out side-effects of drinking supernatural blood...</div> </div> </div> </div>Would Mummies also fall under that interpretation of Unnatural Affinity? And either way, what sort of Condition could it inflict? Sybaris? Obsession keyed to the Arisen/Deceived/Shuankhsen that the vampire fed upon?<br /> <br /> That said, I'm liking your ideas for the effects of supernatural blood on vampires. It's simple and effective, in my opinion. For Prometheans, though, I'm wondering if I should stick to the 1E tidbit on feeding on them, seeing as your idea <i>is</i> a bit complicated for me. Though perhaps you could simplify it somehow as a Condition/Tilt in itself?<br /> <br /> With regards to Beasts, what if drinking the blood of one induces heightened feelings of hunger to the vampire? Represented by the Starved Condition? Alternatively, drinking Vitae taken from one of the Begotten could turn the vampire's next daysleep into Torpor, due to the Beast's connection to the Primordial Dream?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T07:37:36-07:00","id":925888,"title":"","content":"The Promethean core book (can't recall the exact page) said their blood provided half the amount of vitae as a mortal, and tasted foul; also that biting a Promethean didn't tigger a Kiss. So feeding on them was decidedly not worth it.<br /> <br /> Changelings IIRC just tasted weird based on their kith.<br /> <br /> Geist didn't have a canon effect, but I always had their blood provide 1.5 times normal vitae, with a penalty to rotschreck similar to werewolf blood's penalty to frenzy. Also, every health level lost cost the sineater a point of plasm (because the book described their blood as containing some of it).<br /> <br /> For beasts, I go with something outre. If the vampire drinks more than the beast's current satiety level in vitae, they get infected with the beast's Hunger, in place of their own. It doesn't change what they need to survive, but it does change what stirs the vampire's own Beast and threatens wassail.<br /> <br /> For mummies, I usually say no effects good or bad, including no blood, until the mummy has grown a sahu. At that point, it's Christmas: the vitae is multiplied by half the mummy's current Sekhem, and is <i>not</i> limited by the vampire's usual maximum pool. However, as long as they have more vitae than they can hold, the mummy's Judge knows about the vampire, and can bind them to its final purpose. (Ie, every time they see the requisite sin and fail to punish it, they get a Descent-style roll appplied to their willpower).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 07-04-2016, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}